              "files": [
                "internal/tui/model.go"
              ],
              "summary": "progressReceiver comment overstates the nil-case synthesis",
              "intent": "The progressReceiver field comment at internal/tui/model.go:237 ends \"when nil, Init synthesizes it\", unqualified, but only the PageLoading branch synthesizes a BootstrapCompleteMsg for a nil receiver (:1559-1567); the commandPending branch (:1552-1553) and the default branch (:1569-1570) synthesize nothing. Replacing the clause with \"when nil, the loading branch synthesizes it\" narrows the field's own contract to what Init does. Provenance checked: the comment text dates to commit 915e7fcbb (2026-08-11), a month before this work unit began (1ea439825, 2026-09-10), and both non-synthesizing routes existed in Init before it — this change-set's task 10-1 restructured the if-chain into a switch without introducing the wrong claim. The behaviour belongs to the cold-path startup flip.",
              "fails": "A maintainer reading the field's own doc while working the command-pending route concludes every nil-receiver model gets a synthesized terminal event, and synthesizing one on that branch is exactly what the warm command-pending route must not have."
            }
          ],
